CHAPTER.VERS:
And Saul's slaves spoke those words in the ears of David. And David said, Does it seem to you

          {+}
         a light thing to be the king's son-in-law, seeing that I am a poor man, and lightly esteemed?

And Saul said, Thus you

          {+}
         will say to David, The king does not desire any dowry, but a hundred foreskins of the Philistines, to be avenged of the king's enemies. Now Saul thought to make David fall by the hand of the Philistines.
